# Glitch — 140 bpm, F minor. A demo of the glitch inserts: the beat
# repeat (stutter), the reverser and the tape stop, on one track
# (`automate kick.stutter`) or across the whole mix bus (`automate
# stutter`, no track).
#
#   beats  0-8    LOOP   kick-bass, hats, claps and a chord stab
#   beats  8-16   ROLL   the stab plays backwards in quarter-note slices
#                        (each beat is the beat before it, reversed); in
#                        the last bar the kick at beat 12 rolls: caught
#                        and repeated as 1/8, 1/16, 1/32, then 1/64 notes
#   beats 16-24   DROP   the loop again; the whole mix catches on a 1/16
#                        at beat 22, then a 1/32
#   beats 24-28   STOP   the deck loses power: the mix winds down to
#                        silence over 3 beats

bpm 140
gate 0.9
tail 1

section LOOP 0..8
section ROLL 8..16
section DROP 16..24
section STOP 24..28

automate reverb_wet
0.12
automate reverb_decay
0.6
automate tape_drive
0.25
automate comp_in
1
automate comp_threshold
-14

track kick patch=hardkick vel=0.95 gain=1.1
(F1 F1 F1 F1 | F1 F1 G#1 F1)x3 | F1 F1 F1 F1
automate kick.stutter
0 >12 8 >13 16 >14 32 >15 64 >16 0

track hats kit=909 len=0.5 gain=0.8
(R CH R CH R CH R OH)x7

track claps kit=hats len=1
(R CP R CP)x7

track stab patch=pulsechord vel=0.7 gain=0.55 reverb_send=0.25
([F3 G#3 C4]:0.5 R:1 [F3 G#3 C4]:0.5 R:0.5 [D#3 G3 A#3]:1.5 | [C#3 F3 G#3]:0.5 R:1 [C#3 F3 G#3]:0.5 R:0.5 [C3 D#3 G3]:1.5)x3 | [F3 G#3 C4]:4
automate stab.reverse
0 >8 4 >16 0

automate stutter
0 >22 16 >23 32 >24 0
automate tape_stop
0 >25 3
